  "description": "Every degenerate shape the eight endpoints can hand back, in one run, proving each is absorbed and that the walk reaches the good records at the end. network/configuration answers a list rather than an object, so the hostname must fall back to the one on system/info and be split into a short name and a domain. The interface list holds a bare string, an interface whose state is a string rather than an object -- which still has usable addresses on its top-level aliases -- and an interface carrying a multicast MAC and an APIPA address, neither of which identifies anything, so that interface must vanish entirely rather than become a correlator. /pool answers an object where the collection contract promises an array. A disk row is a string, another reports the SMBIOS placeholder 'To be filled by O.E.M.' as its serial and null as its model. One app has no name, one has a string where active_workloads belongs, and one publishes host port 0. Two VM rows must be dropped for different reasons: one has a null id, and one has neither a NIC nor a name that is shaped like a DNS name -- 'Windows 11 Desktop' is an operator's label, and importing it as a hostname would invite runZero to correlate two unrelated guests that happen to share it. The release is also reported as 25.04, which must raise the REST-deprecation warning. Response shapes follow the TrueNAS middleware API models; all data is synthetic.",
